"""R15 tool-api-streaming-blocking gate driver, launched only by the sealed R15 suite.

The driver starts one fresh, owned, target-only server in the immutable release container. That server runs
the sealed tool-call launch contract: C1, interactive w4096 chunking, BF16 KV, no speculation, the
`qwen3_coder` tool parser and the checkpoint-native chat template. The driver proves that process with the
suite's `verify_live_server` before and after the requests. Against it, it sends the sealed
`tool_eval_runaway_microgate` case to `/v1/chat/completions`, as real SSE and then real blocking requests.

Every wire check is the microgate's own code, loaded by pinned SHA-256 and called unchanged: request
construction, HTTP capture, the strict SSE parser with tool-call delta assembly, the blocking parser, the
privacy and wire-shape validation, the stream-versus-blocking comparison, and the server-rendered prompt
digest. The driver adds the runtime binding that the microgate's own live mode deliberately leaves unproven.
It never ingests a prior report, never accepts a PASS flag, and never synthesizes a missing proof.
See R16_TOOL_API_GATE_DRIVER.md.
"""

